WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.181
In 1898, Emperor Guangxu resolved to carry out reforms.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.300
He was influenced by scholars such as Kang Youwei.

00:00:06.621 --> 00:00:09.336
Kang Youwei's memorial was written both long and urgent.

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:13.341
Kang Youwei and Liang Qichao put forward many new ideas.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.610
The reforms covered education, administration, and the economy.

00:00:16.908 --> 00:00:20.012
The young Liang Qichao spoke with great passion.

00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:24.103
New-style schools were opened, and the students were very excited.

00:00:24.521 --> 00:00:26.839
People everywhere were discussing the future of the country.

00:00:27.135 --> 00:00:29.945
But the conservative ministers strongly opposed it.

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:32.762
They believed the changes were coming far too fast.

00:00:33.292 --> 00:00:36.228
The atmosphere in the corridors grew more tense day by day.

00:00:36.805 --> 00:00:39.395
This reform lasted only about one hundred days.

00:00:39.855 --> 00:00:42.665
In the end, Empress Dowager Cixi seized power once again.

00:00:43.218 --> 00:00:46.102
The great hall was completely quiet, with only sighs remaining.

00:00:46.697 --> 00:00:49.543
Many of the reform measures were also revoked.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:53.028
But the seeds of seeking renewal and change had already been sown.

00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:55.600
Sunlight shone on the children's smiling faces.
